[h2]Build 0.9.140[/h2]
[h3]Changed[/h3]
[list]
[*]Repairing gear whose materials cannot be worked out at all (no cost on the item and no recipe that makes it) now takes generic materials for its tech era: leather for neolithic apparel, cloth for medieval and industrial apparel, steel for weapons, plasteel for spacer gear and better - or simply wood logs or steel when the item is plainly wood (bows, clubs, staffs) or metal. Industrial ranged weapons also take a component, and ultra-tech gear an advanced component. Amounts follow the item's value and the damage, like any repair.
[/list]
